### What is the Spring Boot startup flow?

The Spring Boot startup sequence has eight steps that execute in a specific order. Understanding this order helps you debug startup failures and know exactly when your beans, controllers, and scheduled tasks become active.

1. The `main` method calls `SpringApplication.run(MainClass.class, args)`.
2. Spring creates the `ApplicationContext` (the IoC container). For web applications this is `AnnotationConfigServletWebServerApplicationContext`.
3. Auto-configuration kicks in: Spring Boot scans the classpath, finds libraries like Tomcat, JPA, and Redis, and registers matching `@Configuration` classes.
4. `@ComponentScan` discovers all `@Component`, `@Service`, `@Repository`, and `@Controller` classes and registers them as bean definitions.
5. Singleton beans are instantiated in dependency order: constructor injection first, then `@PostConstruct` lifecycle callbacks.
6. The embedded web server (Tomcat by default) is created and started.
7. `CommandLineRunner` and `ApplicationRunner` beans execute their one-time tasks.
8. `ApplicationReadyEvent` is published: the application is fully started and ready to serve requests.

```java
package com.bank;

import org.springframework.boot.SpringApplication;
import org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.SpringBootApplication;

@SpringBootApplication
public class NationalBankApplication {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Step 1: triggers the entire startup sequence
        SpringApplication.run(NationalBankApplication.class, args);
    }
}
```

```java
package com.bank.startup;

import org.springframework.boot.CommandLineRunner;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;
import org.slf4j.Logger;
import org.slf4j.LoggerFactory;

@Component
public class CacheWarmupRunner implements CommandLineRunner {

    private static final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(CacheWarmupRunner.class);

    private final ExchangeRateService rateService;

    public CacheWarmupRunner(ExchangeRateService rateService) {
        this.rateService = rateService;
    }

    @Override
    public void run(String... args) {
        // Step 7: executes after all beans are created and server is started
        log.info("Warming exchange rate cache for National Bank of India");
        rateService.loadAllRates();
        log.info("Cache warmup complete");
    }
}
```

